  "question": {
    "html": "<p>When the speed of sound in a pipe is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"c_{1}\"></span>, the frequency of the first harmonic in the pipe is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"f_{1}\"></span> and the wavelength is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\lambda_{1}\"></span>. Then the speed of sound is changed to <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"c_{2}\"></span>, so that <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"c_{1}&gt;c_{2}\"></span>. The frequency and the wavelength of the first harmonic after the change are <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"f_{1}\"></span> and <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\lambda_{1}\"></span>. How do the wavelengths and the frequencies compare before and after the change?</p>\n\n<table>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td></td>\n<td>\n<p><strong>Wavelengths</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td>\n<p><strong>Frequencies</strong></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-label=\"A\">\n<td><strong>A.</strong></td>\n<td><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\lambda_{1}=\\lambda_{2}\"></span></td>\n<td><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"f_{1}&gt;f_{2}\"></span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-label=\"B\">\n<td><strong>B.</strong></td>\n<td><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\lambda_{1}=\\lambda_{2}\"></span></td>\n<td><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"f_{1}=f_{2}\"></span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-label=\"C\">\n<td><strong>C.</strong></td>\n<td><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\lambda_{1}&gt;\\lambda_{2}\"></span></td>\n<td><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"f_{1}&gt;f_{2}\"></span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-label=\"D\">\n<td><strong>D.</strong></td>\n<td><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\lambda_{1}&gt;\\lambda_{2}\"></span></td>\n<td><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"f_{1}=f_{2}\"></span></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>"
  },
